usage: latency_predictor.py [-h] --configs CONFIGS
                            [--dataset-path DATASET_PATH]
                            [--lat-dataset-path LAT_DATASET_PATH]
                            [--feature-norm FEATURE_NORM [FEATURE_NORM ...]]
                            [--lat-norm LAT_NORM] [--feature-dim FEATURE_DIM]
                            [--hidden-dim HIDDEN_DIM]
                            [--hidden-layer-num HIDDEN_LAYER_NUM]
                            [--ckpt-path CKPT_PATH]
                            [--train-steps TRAIN_STEPS] [--bsz BSZ] [--lr LR]

optional arguments:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --configs CONFIGS
  --dataset-path DATASET_PATH
  --lat-dataset-path LAT_DATASET_PATH
                        the path to read latency dataset
  --feature-norm FEATURE_NORM [FEATURE_NORM ...]
                        normalizing factor for each feature
  --lat-norm LAT_NORM   normalizing factor for latency
  --feature-dim FEATURE_DIM
                        dimension of feature vector
  --hidden-dim HIDDEN_DIM
                        hidden dimension of FC layers in latency predictor
  --hidden-layer-num HIDDEN_LAYER_NUM
                        number of FC layers
  --ckpt-path CKPT_PATH
                        path to save latency predictor weights
  --train-steps TRAIN_STEPS
                        latency predictor training steps
  --bsz BSZ             latency predictor training batch size
  --lr LR               latency predictor training learning rate

Args that start with '--' can also be set in a config file (specified via
--configs). Config file syntax allows: key=value, flag=true, stuff=[a,b,c]
(for details, see syntax at https://goo.gl/R74nmi). In general, command-line
values override config file values which override defaults.
